    {
      "section": "time.clock",
      "confidence": "low",
      "note": "Used '{h} na kaloko' for the hour and an additive '... ka <minutes> na miniti' for minutes (ka = and, miniti = minute), with Fijian numerals (tini ka lima 15, ruasagavulu 20, tolusagavulu 30, vāsagavulu 40, limasagavulu 50). I did not use a 'past/to' construction or 'veimama' for :30 because I could not confirm the idiomatic syntax; the result is long and reads like a careful literal statement rather than casual speech. Native review advised. Specific doubts: (1) Fijian likely has a real 'past/to' idiom (something like 'sivia' = past, 'vo' = remaining) that I could not pin down, so the additive form may sound stilted; (2) ':30' should probably use 'veimama' (half) rather than 'tolusagavulu na miniti'; (3) whether 'ka' is the right conjunction between the hour and the minutes."
    }
  ]
